Project Overview
This project was developed as a sales training solution for Nissan dealership sales consultants. The training focuses specifically on the 2026 Nissan Z Heritage Edition and teaches learners how to position the vehicle emotionally, competitively, and strategically during customer interactions. The course applies gamification, storytelling, multimedia learning, and scenario-based instruction to create a modern automotive sales training experience. Learners progress through three modules while earning visual upgrades to a virtual Nissan Z vehicle as part of a badge progression system.
Learning Objectives
By the end of the training, learners will be able to:
Module 1: Sell The Legacy
* Identify the historical significance of the Nissan Z Heritage Edition
* Recognize unique Heritage Edition design features
* Apply storytelling techniques to emotionally engage customers
Module 2: Know Your Weapon
* Compare the Nissan Z against competitors including the Toyota Supra and Ford Mustang
* Explain the value proposition of the Nissan Z
* Identify engine sound and performance differences between competitors
Module 3: Close The Deal
* Differentiate among Nissan Z trim levels
* Explain Heritage Edition package pricing and value
* Recommend appropriate trims based on customer profiles and budgets
Target Audience
The primary audience for this training includes Nissan sales consultants working at dealerships.
Learner Characteristics
* Ages approximately 25–55
* Minimum one year of automotive sales experience
* Familiarity with Nissan products
* Limited knowledge of advanced Z Heritage Edition sales strategies
* Preference for short, visual, and interactive training experiences
Learning Environment
* The course was designed for:
* Self-paced asynchronous learning
* Mobile and desktop access
* Fast-paced dealership work environments
* Interrupted learning sessions with resume capability
